  nonce: '0392'  # 0392
  message: "Headline (config_info drops package identity name/version/license for 3/11 manifests) is behaviorally DISSOLVED by WI-lirub (commit 2b6387d23a, 2026-07-11): the heuristic extractor gained a monorepo packages/ scan + per-package LICENSE detection, and the pyproject parser now emits name/version/license directly. LIVE REPRO (2026-07-21, closure-evidence): surveyed a manifest-bearing repo -> config_info contains `pyproject.toml: name: acme-widget; version: 2.3.4; license: ...` + `LICENSE: Apache`. Stale filing literal (version 0.5.1) confirmed superseded (0.6.0). Sole residual is cosmetic — the embedding appendix appends a fragmentary chunk and the pyproject license VALUE is clipped mid-token — on a zero-external-consumer x-internal cache (schema x-internal:true). Per the G9 Recommended close-out (owner 2026-07-21), that cosmetic `_build_context_chunk` cleanup is deliberately NOT pursued (not worth the cold-slice CI tax); it is the same surface tracked under WI-samif Part 2 (downgraded). Filed defect resolved -> done."  # 0392
